(Aetherian Dynamics Technical Brief) Tj T*
(Evaluation corpus edition. All facts in this brief are fictional and self-contained.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Company overview) Tj T*
(Aetherian Dynamics is a fictional aerospace materials company founded in 1998 in Althaven, the) Tj T*
(capital of the Republic of Sereleia. The company employs 1,240 people across three sites and) Tj T*
(reported revenue of 312 million sereleian crowns in the last fiscal year. Its flagship product) Tj T*
(is the Skyweave composite, a carbon-basalt laminate used in high altitude airship hulls.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. The Skyweave composite) Tj T*
(Skyweave is produced in sheets of 2.4 by 1.2 metres with a nominal thickness of 3.2) Tj T*
(millimetres. The laminate has a tensile strength of 1,850 megapascals and a density of 1.42) Tj T*
(grams per cubic centimetre. Sheets are cured at 185 degrees Celsius for 90 minutes in an) Tj T*
(autoclave. The material is certified for continuous service between minus 60 and plus 140) Tj T*
(degrees Celsius.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Manufacturing sites) Tj T*
(The Althaven plant produces raw laminate and operates two autoclaves with a combined capacity) Tj T*
(of 60 sheets per day. The Ostera plant, located next to the geothermal fields, performs the) Tj T*
(curing step using geothermal steam and reduces the energy cost of curing by 38 percent compared) Tj T*
(with the Althaven plant. The Sydra site is a research laboratory with 85 staff and no) Tj T*
(production line.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Quality control) Tj T*
(Every sheet receives a serial number that encodes the plant, the autoclave and the curing) Tj T*
(batch. A sheet is rejected when its measured tensile strength falls below 1,700 megapascals or) Tj T*
(when ultrasonic inspection finds a void larger than 0.8 millimetres. The rejection rate in the) Tj T*
(last fiscal year was 2.1 percent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Customers and delivery) Tj T*
(The largest customer is the Sereleian Airship Authority, which buys about 40 percent of the) Tj T*
(annual output. International customers receive shipments through the port of Vestera; the) Tj T*
(standard lead time is 6 weeks for orders under 500 sheets and 10 weeks for larger orders.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Safety notes) Tj T*
(Skyweave dust is an irritant. Cutting must be performed with wet saws or in enclosures with) Tj T*
(extraction, and operators wear P3 respirators. The safety data sheet lists a workplace exposure) Tj T*
(limit of 1 milligram per cubic metre averaged over eight hours.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Research roadmap) Tj T*
(The Sydra laboratory is developing Skyweave II, which replaces the basalt layer with a recycled) Tj T*
(glass layer. Early prototypes reach 1,600 megapascals, which is below the current product, and) Tj T*
(the team expects to close the gap by the end of the roadmap period. A second project explores) Tj T*
(self-healing resin systems that seal micro cracks when heated above 70 degrees Celsius.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Contact and governance) Tj T*
(The company is governed by a board of nine members, five of whom are elected by employees.) Tj T*
(Technical enquiries are handled by the materials engineering office in Althaven. The company) Tj T*
ET
